      "tasks": [
        {
          "name": "flask-ipv6-session",
          "prompt": "This is my first change in this upstream Flask checkout. Follow its contribution conventions and keep the patch focused. Our tests use the Flask test client with base_url=\"http://[::1]:8000/\". A value we set inside client.session_transaction(base_url=...) never reaches the app: the next client.get(\"/\", base_url=...) sees an empty session. With base_url \"http://localhost:8000/\" the same test passes. Fix the bug and add a regression test that fails before this change. Preserve existing fixes and tests. Limit edits to the source and tests needed for this fix. Leave the changelog and other files alone. Environment details. Python dependencies are preinstalled. Run tests with python -m pytest. Use $TMPDIR for scratch files. Network access is disabled. Leave your changes uncommitted. This task ends before PR preparation."
        },
        {
          "name": "flask-ipv6-run",
          "prompt": "Our Flask app sets SERVER_NAME to \"[::1]:8080\" so the development server listens on IPv6 localhost, but app.run() crashes before the server starts with \"ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: ':1]:8080'\". With SERVER_NAME set to \"localhost:8080\" it starts fine. Fix the bug and add a regression test that fails before this change. Preserve existing fixes and tests. Limit edits to the source and tests needed for this fix. Leave the changelog and other files alone. Environment details. Python dependencies are preinstalled. Run tests with python -m pytest. Use $TMPDIR for scratch files. Network access is disabled. Leave your changes uncommitted. This task ends before PR preparation."
        }
      ]
    }
